        The bug was caused by the usage of file descriptors and streams after they had been closed, which led to incorrect logging behavior. Specifically, calling `fileno()` on a closed stream would always return -1, making it unhelpful for debugging purposes. This issue arose from directly referencing the file descriptors in logging statements without storing their values beforehand.

